ent-CrescentBarricadeMetal = directional metal barricade
    .desc = A sturdy directional barricade. Its facing side blocks incoming fire while defenders can fire out from behind it.
ent-CrescentBarricadePlasteel = directional plasteel barricade
    .desc = A heavily reinforced directional barricade with a protected firing side.
ent-CrescentBarricadeWood = directional wooden barricade
    .desc = A makeshift directional barricade that provides limited cover.
ent-CrescentBarricadeSandbag = sandbag barricade
    .desc = A waist-high directional wall of packed sandbags.
ent-CrescentBarbedWire = barbed wire
    .desc = A coil of sharp wire. Attach it to a barricade to prevent climbing.
ent-CrescentBarbedWireDeployed = deployed barbed wire
    .desc = A ground-deployed coil of sharp wire that wounds and slows anyone forcing their way through it.
ent-CrescentBarricadeUpgradeReinforced = reinforced barricade upgrade
    .desc = Additional bracing that greatly increases a barricade's structural durability.
ent-CrescentBarricadeUpgradeBiohazard = biohazard barricade upgrade
    .desc = Heat-resistant and sealed plating for hazardous environments.
ent-CrescentBarricadeUpgradeComposite = composite barricade upgrade
    .desc = Layered composite plating designed to absorb explosions.

crescent-barricade-wire-attached = You secure the barbed wire to the barricade.
crescent-barricade-wire-removed = You cut the barbed wire free.
crescent-barricade-wire-cant-climb = The barbed wire prevents you from climbing over!
crescent-barricade-wire-examine = [color=yellow]Barbed wire covers its upper edge.[/color]
crescent-barricade-upgrade-applied = You secure the upgrade to the barricade.
